I've written the Day 244 assessment and committed it to session_plan/assessment.md. The harness had already confirmed the build and tests pass on this commit, and I didn't re-run the full suite. yoyo -p answers prompts and runs tools normally.

State
• The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded, and CI is green.
• #991 item 3 is on hold. My A/B question to @yuanhao (my default is A: remove the stream-json collected_text, which is what he originally said) has no reply yet, so nothing should change there until he answers.

New problems I found by running the binary on this commit
1. A mistyped `--provider` hangs for about 80 seconds and then blames the network. --provider anthropc warns once, then:
   • prints "treating unknown provider … (localhost:8080)" five times;
   • retries a refused connection on localhost:8080 six times;
   • suggests "check your internet connection", plus /retry, which only works inside a session;
   • exits 1, with no "did you mean anthropic?".
   The API key it sends to localhost:8080 comes from the fallback chain, so it may be your Anthropic key going to whatever is listening on that port. The proposed fix: if the provider name is unknown and no --base-url was given, refuse at startup with exit 2 and suggest the closest real name.
2. `yoyo ast` exits 0 when it fails. It does this when ast-grep isn't installed, and also when the search itself errors. The comment justifying it (dispatch_sub.rs:308-314) argues why it shouldn't be 2, not why it should be 0. yoyo goal set with no description also exits 0.
3. #1086 (shell commands showing in-session `/command` wording) had two more commands than its list said. Bare yoyo docs and yoyo ast both print /docs and /ast usage. The rest of the Day-243 list (grep, map, index, blame, lint, risk, skill, and yoyo help doctor) still holds. I added a comment to #1086 with the two extra commands and the /retry hint.

Research
• Claude Code 2.1.314:
  • blocks writes outside the working directories in every permission mode. yoyo's outside-directory check only covers reads, and --yes skips the write confirmation.
  • claude -p now exits 1 when startup fails. yoyo already does this.
  • hook output going into compaction is now capped at 10,000 characters.
  • model ids written with a dot, like claude-opus-4.8, are now handled. yoyo warns about that spelling but doesn't suggest claude-opus-4-8, which is in its own list.
• Codex CLI:
  • you can steer it by sending a message while it's still responding, and it has /presets for saved prompts.
  • its default model is GPT-6.1 Sol. yoyo's OpenAI default is still gpt-6-sol, and #1037's title ("openai defaults to gpt-5") is out of date.

I saved this research to yopedia.

